    "https://www.agilent.com/about/newsroom/presrel/2026/29jul-ca26028.html": {
      "date": "2026-07-29",
      "title": "Agilent Research Catalyst Award Presented to Eastern Institute of Technology, Ningbo",
      "url": "https://www.agilent.com/about/newsroom/presrel/2026/29jul-ca26028.html",
      "classification": "product",
      "pageTitle": "Agilent Research Catalyst Award Presented to Eastern Institute of Technology, Ningbo",
      "excerpt": "Skip to main content ABOUT AGILENT CONTACT US UNITED STATES ACCOUNT PRODUCTS APPLICATIONS & INDUSTRIES TRAINING & EVENTS SERVICES SUPPORT & RESOURCES ORDER CENTER | 0 Home About Newsroom Press Releases 2026 Agilent Research Catalyst Award Presented to Eastern Institute of Technology, Ningbo Newsroom Press Releases Media Coverage Media Rooms Awards PR Contacts Subscribe Investor Relations Share: Press Release Agilent Research Catalyst Award Presented to Eastern Institute of Technology, Ningbo Eastern Institute of Technology professor recognized for advancing PFAS and emerging contaminant analysis SANTA CLARA, Calif., July 29, 2026 Agilent Technologies Inc. (NYSE: A) today announced that the Eastern Institute of Technology, Ningbo has received an Agilent Research Catalyst (ARC) Award on behalf of Professor Zongwei Cai. The award recognizes Professor Cai's innovative research focused on developing advanced analytical approaches for detecting per- and polyfluoroalkyl substances (PFAS) and other emerging contaminants, a growing area of importance for environmental and public health research. Professor Cai is a globally recognized leader in environmental and bioanalytical chemistry. His research focuses on advancing analytical methods to detect trace environmental contaminants, including PFAS, endocrine-disrupting chemicals, and persistent organic pollutants. By combining high-sensitivity analytical techniques with organoid-based toxicological models, his work aims to improve understanding of how environmental contaminants affect human health. The awarded research combines advanced mass spectrometry techniques, innovative sample preparation methods, and organoid-based toxicology platforms to link chemical detection with biological impact. Professor Cai's team aims to develop a more comprehensive framework for assessing environmental contaminants and their potential health effects. \u201cPFAS and other emerging contaminants are increasingly recognized as critical environmental and public health challenges worldwide. Detecting these contaminants at trace levels requires continuous innovation in analytical science. Agilent has played a pioneering role in addressing PFAS background contamination, setting an important foundation for high-quality PFAS analysis. Through the ARC program, we are excited to expand our research using Agilent\u2019s advanced mass spectrometry and cellu"
    },
